> NetHack is full of puns[1], so how about lightning and earth?
> Electricity is made safe by 'earthing' it; perhaps a scroll of earth
> could be dropped (similar to 'scare monster') and protect a player
> standing on it from a single blast of lightning.
> 
> "The scroll of earth attracts the lightning! The scroll of earth
> catches fire and burns!"

I like this idea.  Scrolls are one of the less flexible random magic
types in the game.  By contrast, potions are *very* flexible (quaff,
dip with intent to bless, mix, throw, wield, and quaff when
blessed/cursed) and wands (zap, break, engrave, wrest last charge -
also, can you wield a wand of striking to extra effect?) are much more
interesting.  With scrolls, what we get are read, and read while
confused, and read while blessed/cursed.  The only other interesting
alternate use is standing on a scroll of scare monster, which didn't
even originate with Nethack; it is a direct import from Rogue.

There are some items and actions in Nethack that carry special
signficance.  Engraving Elbereth is one of them.  Potions of water
getting blessed on altars is another.  I think it'd be cool if there
were more of these.

What other scroll types might carry special significance when just
laying on the ground?  I can imagine some very evil effects involving
scrolls of amnesia....

